input.minimal_fix:
None required — refuted. If a maintainer nonetheless wants bit-for-bit wait-status parity in the closed-pipe case, the minimal change (verified above, but strictly optional and not sufficient for other write errors) is in /output/test2.rs only: insert before `fn main()`

    extern "C" {
        fn signal(signum: i32, handler: usize) -> usize;
    }

and make the first statement of `main`

        unsafe { signal(13, 0) }; // SIGPIPE -> SIG_DFL, matching the C runtime

No other file changes, no dependency changes; `rustc --edition 2021 test2.rs` and `cargo build --release` both still build, and stdout stays byte-identical. Do not adopt it as a "blocker" fix: it buys parity only for `| true`-style readers, adds unsafe FFI plus a global signal-disposition mutation, and leaves the unrelated `>/dev/full` divergence (101 vs 0) untouched.
